# held/civil/stick: the walking stick (art weapon 9): a cane with a crook and an iron ferrule (PROPS, P2b). Elders and
# refugees lean on it. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. The wood is the leather ramp drawn light (outline, highlight core), so
# it parts from the boots and takes the person's wood (six by person). It rides the legs channel on the pivot, a drawing
# per frame, so the tip is PLANTED: in the side views it strikes ahead as the hand swings forward and stays on its spot of
# ground for four frames while the body walks over it (3 px a frame against the pivot, as the feet), then swings through
# lifted. Front and back: the crook under the fist, upright, lifted a pixel when the hand rises. It sits under armNear, so
# the near hand (front, right and left views) is drawn over its crook; from behind it stands behind the body. In the left
# view it changes to the near (left) hand, so a stick always shows (a cane is no weapon: STYLE_P2 9's right hand is for arms).
# While a posture busies the hands (the flag "posture") it is set down: leaning on the right thigh where the legs stand
# (legs idle), gone otherwise. "lie": it lies along the dead body by the hand.
# (MOTION_P2 7.5, fix r1) the side walk keeps the cane OFF the legs: its tip plants in the gaps between the footprints
# (10 px ahead of the pivot at walkC, then 7 / 4 / 1: the 3 / 3 / 3 advance), so it strikes a pixel ahead of the leading
# toe, passes in front of the planted shin, and stands in the gap between the legs at walkA; it lifts there (walkA2,
# still between the legs) and swings through with the passing legs (walkB2). Its crook (a cap curling forward, the drooping
# end a pixel ahead) sits under the hand; her hand is a row higher, so her views are a row taller.
# (fix r2) at the passes (walkB2 lifted, walkD2 planted) the shaft stands upright in the 1-2 px channel between the planted
# shin and the passing boot (its outlines shared with theirs), stepping forward only in its last rows to the ferrule, so it
# never crosses the passing heel; at walkC (both facings) its last shaft rows ride a pixel ahead, off the raised toe. In the run the cane
# is carried, never planted: in the gap between the legs while the fist swings back (run1, run6), trailing behind the
# straight legs at the push (run2, run5), swung up ahead with the fist (run3, run4).
# (fix r3, R3-07) the walk's new pass (legs/adult/loco/std.pxm: the swing boot lifted BEHIND the planted heel, the
# owner's reference frame 3) opens the column in front of the planted shin, so both passes stand there, off every boot:
# walkD2 planted at +4 (the 3 / 3 / 3 plant kept: +10 / +7 / +4 / +1), a straight 2 px lean (+2 / +3 / +4, steps at the
# knee row and F-3) with an air column between the stick and the shin; walkB2 lifted 1 and swinging through, the tip
# leading at +5 (a 3 px lean, a step every 2 rows) between the gap at walkA2 and the plant at walkC. Her views are the
# same drawing a row taller (her hand). Her run2 / run5 L take his trailing stick (as her R views do): her own L views
# stood the stick upright through her planted boot.
use person
body man woman
role held stick
layer neck
anchor pivot
keys legs
z 40

